.TH GARAGEJAM 1 "October 2026" "@PACKAGE_NAME@ @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
garagejam \- multitrack music recording studio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B garagejam
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [\fIPROJECT.gjxml\fR...]
.br
.B garagejam
\fB\-\-export\-mixdown\fR=\fIPROJECT.gjxml\fR [\fB\-\-output\fR=\fIOUT.wav\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B GarageJam
records music track by track. Arm a track, press record, and play along
with the tracks you already have. Each track has volume, pan, mute and
solo controls that can be changed while the jam is playing, and the
finished jam can be exported as a stereo WAV mixdown.
.PP
Projects are saved in the GarageJam XML format (GJXML). Recorded takes
are 16\-bit PCM WAV files stored next to the project file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-export\-mixdown =\fIPROJECT.gjxml\fR
Render the project to a WAV file without opening a window, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIOUT.wav\fR
File name for \fB\-\-export\-mixdown\fR. Defaults to
\fIPROJECT\fR\-mixdown.wav.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
GStreamer options such as \fB\-\-gst\-debug\-level\fR are also accepted.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Record into the armed track (a new track is created if none is armed)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Space
Play / stop
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Add track
.TP
.B Ctrl+I
Import audio
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Export mixdown
.TP
.BR Ctrl+N ", " Ctrl+O ", " Ctrl+S ", " Ctrl+Shift+S
New, open, save, save as
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Music/GarageJam/
Default folder for takes of jams that have not been saved yet.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gst\-launch\-1.0 (1)
.PP
@PACKAGE_URL@
.SH AUTHOR
Ole Kristian Aamot <ole.aamot@aamotinnovation.com>
